# CODEOWNERS — auto-request review on security-sensitive paths.
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection for these
# paths to actually block merge — the file alone only requests review.

# CI, build scripts, and the Electron desktop app all execute code with
# elevated privileges (GITHUB_TOKEN write access, contents on the maintainer's
# disk via saveIcon IPC). A malicious PR touching these paths could persist.
/.github/         @pphatdev

# Registry manifests drive what the CLI installs into consumer projects —
# a bad merge here fans out to every downstream user.
/index.json       @pphatdev
/brands.json      @pphatdev
/regular.json     @pphatdev
/schema.json      @pphatdev
/config.json      @pphatdev
